Information 

How pipeline works together: 
	Jenkins  →  Fastlane  →  Xcode / xcodebuild / tests
	- Jenkins says: “Run the CI pipeline”
	- Fastlane says: “Here’s HOW to build and test an iOS app”
	- Xcode does the actual work
 
--------------------------------Setup--------------------------------
 
Install Jenkins (local CI server)
    brew install jenkins-lts
    brew services start jenkins-lts
    
Install fastlane - sudo gem install fastlane
Init fastlane in the project - fastlane init
To test locally using fastlane run - fastlane ci

Create Jenkins Pipeline Job
    Start Jenkins - brew services start jenkins-lts
    Jenkins UI - http://localhost:8080
        New Item
        Name: ios-ci
        Type: Pipeline
        Scroll → Pipeline section
        Definition: Pipeline script from SCM
        SCM: Git
        Repo URL: https://github.com/chamodh98/DiscoverHub.git
        Branch: master
        Script Path: Jenkinsfile
    Add Jenkinsfile (pipeline definition) - then commit and push
    Trigger the pipeline
        In Jenkins Open ios-ci Click Build Now
    To find the Jenkins password run this command - cat ~/.jenkins/secrets/initialAdminPassword

    
Start Jenkins - brew services start jenkins-lts
View Jenkins Dashboard - http://localhost:8080
Shut down Jenkins - brew services stop jenkins-lts




    


